<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?><rss xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" version="2.0"><channel><title>World News, Today World News, Latest International News, World Breaking News, Trending News of World - Times of India</title><link>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world</link><description>World News Today: Read the latest world news headlines, Current International breaking news world wide. In depth analysis and top news headlines world wide.</description><language>en-gb</language><lastBuildDate>2026-08-20T06:48:35+05:30</lastBuildDate><atom:link type="application/rss+xml" rel="self" href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/rssfeeds/296589292.cms"/><copyright>Copyright:(C) Thu, 20 Aug 2026 06:48:35 IST Bennett Coleman &amp; Co. Ltd, http://in.indiatimes.com/policyterms/1554651.cms</copyright><docs>http://syndication.indiatimes.com/</docs><image><title>World News, Today World News, Latest International News, World Breaking News, Trending News of World - Times of India</title><url>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/507610.cms</url><link>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world</link></image><item><title><![CDATA[Meet Audrey Zheng, the 17-year-old Pennsylvania student who developed a...]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133358683.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[A talented high school student has pioneered a cutting-edge bioengineering method for the early detection of pancreatic cancer. By utilizing magnetic beads to isolate tumor-derived particles from blood samples, her clinical trials demonstrated remarkable accuracy. Her extraordinary research has secured her a spot as a national finalist in a prestigious science competition, offering a promising new avenue for timely diagnosis and improved patient survival outcomes.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/meet-audrey-zheng-the-17-year-old-pennsylvania-student-who-developed-a-pancreatic-cancer-test-it-correctly-identified-87-of-patients-and-87-5-without-the-disease/articleshow/133358683.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/meet-audrey-zheng-the-17-year-old-pennsylvania-student-who-developed-a-pancreatic-cancer-test-it-correctly-identified-87-of-patients-and-87-5-without-the-disease/articleshow/133358683.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-20T01:56:39+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133358700,imgsize-563157.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[In 1961, British scientists stopped farming a 4-hectare barley field and left it alone; 60 years later...]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133358523.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[A groundbreaking six-decade study reveals that passive rewilding effectively fosters the development of lush native woodlands. Through protective thorny scrub, young trees thrived, shielded from herbivores, while wind and jays ingeniously spread seeds, outlining the woodlands’ unique patterns. After fifty years, the area began to mirror the characteristics of ancient woodlands, showcasing an eco-friendly and budget-friendly approach to achieving woodland restoration objectives.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/in-1961-british-scientists-stopped-farming-a-4-hectare-barley-field-and-left-it-alone-60-years-later-it-had-turned-itself-into-a-complex-native-woodland/articleshow/133358523.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/in-1961-british-scientists-stopped-farming-a-4-hectare-barley-field-and-left-it-alone-60-years-later-it-had-turned-itself-into-a-complex-native-woodland/articleshow/133358523.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-20T01:37:34+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Science Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133358634,imgsize-852985.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[In 1963, a California builder made a house that rotates 320 degrees using two washing-machine motors]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133354983.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[A remarkable rotating house, built in 1963 by the imaginative Sam Harkleroad, is now available for sale, showcasing a one-of-a-kind design. Overlooking busy Highway 101, this property comprises seven homes, all presently leased, with a total price tag of $3.3 million. Harkleroad's distinctive architectural legacy thrives across Marin County, but his grandson has chosen to list the asset, citing the complexities of maintenance as a challenge.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/real-estate/in-1963-a-california-builder-made-a-house-that-rotates-320-degrees-using-two-washing-machine-motors-63-years-later-it-is-on-the-market-for-the-first-time/articleshow/133354983.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/real-estate/in-1963-a-california-builder-made-a-house-that-rotates-320-degrees-using-two-washing-machine-motors-63-years-later-it-is-on-the-market-for-the-first-time/articleshow/133354983.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-20T00:43:04+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133358200,imgsize-1019892.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Indian caregiver fatally stabbed in Israel, elderly couple’s grandson indicted]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133354364.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/middle-east/indian-caregiver-fatally-stabbed-in-israel-elderly-couples-grandson-indicted/articleshow/133354364.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/middle-east/indian-caregiver-fatally-stabbed-in-israel-elderly-couples-grandson-indicted/articleshow/133354364.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-19T22:40:34+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133354686,imgsize-662735.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[At least 100 killed after illegal gold mine collapses in Central African Republic]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133356183.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/at-least-100-killed-after-illegal-gold-mine-collapses-in-central-african-republic/articleshow/133356183.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/at-least-100-killed-after-illegal-gold-mine-collapses-in-central-african-republic/articleshow/133356183.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-19T23:23:58+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Vijaya Srivastava</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133356287,imgsize-347806.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Meet Natalie Muro, 18-year-old Colorado student who used an invasive plant to fight algal blooms]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133353123.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[A remarkable eighteen-year-old student has developed an ingenious device aimed at eradicating toxic algal blooms. Utilizing wind-driven waves and invasive plant species, this unique system demonstrated impressive results in field tests, removing nearly all cyanobacteria and trapping decayed cell matter. This groundbreaking solution offers a cost-effective way to restore and revitalize unhealthy freshwater ecosystems.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/meet-natalie-muro-the-18-year-old-colorado-student-who-used-wind-driven-waves-and-an-invasive-plant-to-fight-toxic-algal-blooms-in-a-real-reservoir/articleshow/133353123.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/meet-natalie-muro-the-18-year-old-colorado-student-who-used-wind-driven-waves-and-an-invasive-plant-to-fight-toxic-algal-blooms-in-a-real-reservoir/articleshow/133353123.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-19T21:49:36+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133353529,imgsize-760522.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[1958, the US secretly detonated 3 nuclear devices 100–500 km above the South Atlantic]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133352716.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[In a clandestine effort, Operation Argus conducted nuclear tests in the stratosphere over the South Atlantic Ocean. These detonations resulted in spectacular artificial auroras and fleeting radiation belts around our planet. The mission’s intent was to shield against Soviet missile threats and radar detection systems. Yet, the swift vanishing of these barriers caused significant communication disturbances, leading to the formulation of international accords banning nuclear experiments in space.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/1958-the-us-secretly-detonated-3-nuclear-devices-100500-km-above-the-south-atlantic-they-created-artificial-auroras-and-radiation-belts-that-lasted-weeks/articleshow/133352716.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/1958-the-us-secretly-detonated-3-nuclear-devices-100500-km-above-the-south-atlantic-they-created-artificial-auroras-and-radiation-belts-that-lasted-weeks/articleshow/133352716.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-19T21:24:07+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133352923,imgsize-970022.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[A 9-year-old girl in the Philippines raised money to help one of the world's rarest birds]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133342965.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/a-9-year-old-girl-in-the-philippines-raised-money-to-help-one-of-the-worlds-rarest-birds-the-child-became-an-unlikely-conservation-campaigner/articleshow/133342965.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/a-9-year-old-girl-in-the-philippines-raised-money-to-help-one-of-the-worlds-rarest-birds-the-child-became-an-unlikely-conservation-campaigner/articleshow/133342965.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-19T17:20:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133342965,imgsize-79421.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[American photographer who captured one of the earliest images of a total solar eclipse in 1851]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133343714.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-forgotten-american-photographer-captured-one-of-the-